      "narrative": "You ask the question, but Mara's answer is barely a flicker of interest. She doesn't lean in, doesn't weigh your words. The inquiry just... slides off her.\n\n\"Before it was filed?\" She repeats the phrase flatly, as if tasting something sour. \"Couldn't tell you. The gate's been shut for weeks. Whoever had the keys before is long gone, or dead, or doesn't care anymore.\"\n\nShe waves a hand dismissively, already turning back to her drink. \"The lock's been filed clean through. Someone wanted it that way. Past that? Not my business.\"\n\nThe answer is hollow. You sense she's holding back \u2014 or worse, she genuinely doesn't care enough to dig deeper. Either way, the question landed on dead ground.\n\nAcross the room, Toran Vex fumbles with his papers. A single sheet slips from the stack and drifts to the floor near his feet. He doesn't pick it up. His hands are trembling slightly as he gathers the rest, his eyes fixed on the tabletop.\n\nMara notices none of this. She drains her cup and sets it down with a dull clack.\n\n\"Anything else?\" she asks, not looking at you."
    },
