      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the damp morning air, carrying the name of a dead man to a gate that hasn't opened in weeks.\n\n\"Old Bram!\"\n\nThe name echoes faintly off the stone facades of the surrounding buildings, then fades into silence. No answer comes. The arch stands mute, its pale veins catching the grey light. The shimmer beyond it doesn't stir.\n\nThe courier in the travel-stained cloak flinches at your call \u2014 a small, startled motion \u2014 then turns to look at you. Their face is young, sharp-featured, with dark circles under wary eyes. They've been watching you since you arrived, but now their attention sharpens.\n\n\"Bram's dead,\" they say, their voice carrying a note of flat certainty. \"You won't get an answer from him.\"\n\nThey pause, studying you with the same focused attention they gave the arch moments ago.\n\n\"Looking for passage?\""
