      "narrative": "You drop to one knee, sweeping your fingers across the cracked cobbles beneath the arch. Dust, grit, a few scattered pebbles \u2014 nothing that tells a story. The ground beneath the gate is unremarkable, worn smooth by years of feet and weather. If there was ever a clue here about how the gate was breached, it's long been scuffed away or was never visible in the first place.\n\nYou come up empty-handed, your palm coated in nothing but grey dust.\n\nThe courier watches you straighten, a faint crease between their brows. They don't speak, but their posture shifts \u2014 a subtle lean backward, a hand drifting closer to their belt. Your sudden intensity has made them wary.\n\n\"What are you looking for?\" they ask, the question careful, measured. \"The lock's been filed through. That's not exactly subtle work.\""
